      "speaker": "",
      "text": "This yard was a garrison once. The terraces were built for archers, and the bridge between them was the only way across when the lower ground flooded in spring.\n\nWhen the garrison left, they sealed the stores below, but not well. Foxes found the way in first, then the red ones followed, and nobody has been brave or foolish enough to clear them out.\n\n{b}They say{/b} the old quartermaster hid a key somewhere in the cellar, and that the key opens something far more interesting than a store room. I am too old to go and look. You are not.",
      "type": "line"
    },
